# =============================================================================
# What belongs in this repository
#
#   TRACKED : our own source (TAMP, isaacsim, LLM scripts, perception, scripts/),
#             the manuscript and response (_2026__IEEE_Access/), the project docs
#             (CLAUDE.md, PLAN.md, SESSION_LOG.md, REFACTOR.md, ...), the analysis
#             code, and the per-trial batch CSVs -- those CSVs are the paper's data.
#   IGNORED : vendored third-party trees, build outputs, model weights, archives,
#             environments and batch logs. Each block below says how to get it back.
#
# Note: some model checkpoints under LLM/llama/model/checkpoint/ are ALREADY in
# git history. Ignoring the directory stops new ones being added; it does not
# untrack what is committed (that would need a history rewrite, not done here).
# =============================================================================

# --- editors / caches -------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- python environments ----------------------------------------------------
# .venv-sdl is the Isaac Sim 6.0.1 env (~30 GB); uv also writes its own
# .gitignore inside it. Recreate per README / environment.yml.
.venv-sdl/
.venv/
venv/

# --- colcon (ROS 2) build tree ----------------------------------------------
# Regenerate: ros2_isaacsim_ws/build_interfaces.sh (py3.12) and
# colcon build --packages-select tamp_interfaces (conda sdl, py3.10).
build/
install/
log/
ros2_isaacsim_ws/build/
ros2_isaacsim_ws/install/
ros2_isaacsim_ws/log/

# --- randomized-trials batch logs -------------------------------------------
# ~344 MB of Isaac Sim / tamp_server / driver logs per batch. The batch RESULTS
# live in _2026__IEEE_Access/revision/analysis/data/*.csv (tracked), and each
# batch's code-under-test and settings are recorded in its RUN_INFO.txt, which
# is kept.
scripts/trials/logs/**
!scripts/trials/logs/
!scripts/trials/logs/*/
!scripts/trials/logs/**/RUN_INFO.txt

# --- LLM model weights and archives -----------------------------------------
# Fine-tuned adapters / tokenizers / optimizer state. Re-obtain from the
# training scripts in LLM/llama/script/ or the authors' model store.
LLM/llama/model/checkpoint/
LLM/llama/script/experiments/ActionReasoner/model/
# 217 MB duplicate archive of the unpacked ActionReasoner directory, and over
# GitHub's 100 MB per-file limit.
LLM/llama/script/experiments/ActionReasoner.zip

# --- PDDLStream baseline (vendored third party) ------------------------------
# experiments/pddlstream is an upstream checkout: Fast Downward (575 MB, whose
# builds/release/bin/downward is itself over GitHub's 100 MB limit) plus 460 MB
# of PyBullet example models. Only OUR baseline implementation is tracked --
# examples/pybullet/fr5_obstacle, the FR5 problem the paper compares against.
experiments/pddlstream/downward/
experiments/pddlstream/temp/
experiments/pddlstream/examples/**
!experiments/pddlstream/examples/
!experiments/pddlstream/examples/pybullet/
!experiments/pddlstream/examples/pybullet/fr5_obstacle/
!experiments/pddlstream/examples/pybullet/fr5_obstacle/**

# --- vendored simulation assets ---------------------------------------------
# LabUtopia (111 MB) is a third-party asset pack the scene USDs reference by
# relative path (third_party/LabUtopia/...). Not our code; re-obtain upstream.
third_party/

# --- scratch ----------------------------------------------------------------
*.tmp
*.swp
nohup.out
